      "content": "Feeling like you are constantly serving others while your own life fades is an incredibly isolating and draining experience. That persistent dread each morning sounds exhausting, and it's a sign that your needs are not being met. It might be time to look at small, manageable ways to carve out time just for *you*, even if it feels impossible right now. A therapist can provide strategies to help you set boundaries and reclaim some space for your own well-being.",
